@HostAddress = http://localhost:5002
# Usuarios de los datos semilla (UserSeedData), todos con la contraseña MiPassword123!
@MariaId = a1b2c3d4-0000-0000-0000-111122223333
@Password = MiPassword123!

### ---------- Éxito ----------

### Registrar un usuario nuevo → 201 (cambiar el email para repetirlo)
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/users/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nombre": "Ana",
  "apellido": "Martínez",
  "email": "ana@email.com",
  "password": "{{Password}}"
}

### Login correcto → 200
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/users/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "maria@email.com",
  "password": "{{Password}}"
}

### Obtener un usuario por ID → 200
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/users/{{MariaId}}
Accept: application/json

### ---------- Errores ----------

### Email ya registrado → 409 (USR-001)
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/users/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nombre": "María",
  "apellido": "González",
  "email": "maria@email.com",
  "password": "{{Password}}"
}

### Datos inválidos → 400 (USR-002), lista todos los problemas
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/users/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nombre": "",
  "email": "no-es-un-email"
}

### Contraseña incorrecta → 401 (USR-003). Al tercer intento la cuenta se bloquea (D-09)
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/users/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ana@email.com",
  "password": "PasswordIncorrecta1!"
}

### Bloqueado por intentos fallidos → 403 (USR-004)
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/users/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "juan@email.com",
  "password": "{{Password}}"
}

### Bloqueado manualmente (fraude) → 403 (USR-005)
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/users/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "carlos@email.com",
  "password": "{{Password}}"
}

### Usuario inexistente → 404 (USR-007)
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/users/11111111-2222-3333-4444-555555555555
Accept: application/json

### ID que no es un GUID → 404 (USR-007, D-17)
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/users/99
Accept: application/json

### ---------- Observabilidad ----------

### Correlation ID propio: se devuelve en el header y aparece en los logs
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/users/{{MariaId}}
X-Correlation-Id: demo-users-123

### Health checks
GET {{HostAddress}}/health

###
GET {{HostAddress}}/health/ready

###
GET {{HostAddress}}/health/live
